Using Java, write a function that takes an input string and returns the string reversed, but with all punctuation marks removed. The function should also convert all letters to lowercase and remove any duplicate characters. Additionally, the function should be implemented using recursion and have a time complexity of O(n) and a space complexity of O(n), where n is the length of the input string.

### Response:
