```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String input = "Hello, World!";
        String reversed = reverseString(input);
        System.out.println(reversed);
    }

    public static String reverseString(String input) {
        // Base case: if the input string is empty or has only one character, return it as is
        if (input.isEmpty() || input.length() == 1) {
            return input.toLowerCase();
        }

        // Recursive case:
        // Remove the first and last characters from the input string
        String substring = input.substring(1, input.length() - 1);
        substring = substring.replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z]", ""); // Remove punctuation marks

        // Recursively reverse the substring
        String reversed = reverseString(substring);

        // Check if the first character of the original input string exists in the reversed substring
        // If it exists, don't include it in the final reversed string
        if (reversed.indexOf(Character.toLowerCase(input.charAt(0))) != -1) {
            return reversed;
        } else {
            return Character.toLowerCase(input.charAt(0)) + reversed;
        }
    }
}
```

The `reverseString` function takes an input string and recursively reverses it while removing punctuation marks and duplicate characters. It follows the provided time and space complexity requirements. 

