The `calculate_sum(n)` function is another recursive function that calculates the sum of all positive integers up to a given number `n`. It uses a base case (`n == 1`) to stop the recursion and returns 1. Otherwise, it calls itself with the argument `n-1` and adds `n` to the result of the recursive call.

