function flipBinaryTree(root) {
  if (!root) {
    return null;
  }

  // Swap left and right children
  let temp = root.left;
  root.left = root.right;
  root.right = temp;

  // Recursively flip left and right subtrees
  flipBinaryTree(root.left);
  flipBinaryTree(root.right);

  return root;
}
```

This implementation uses recursion to traverse the tree and flip the left and right children of each node. The base case is when the current node is null, in which case we simply return null.

To flip the children of a node, we swap the left and right children using a temporary variable. Then, we recursively call `flipBinaryTree` on the left and right subtrees to flip their children as well.

Finally, we return the root node of the flipped tree.

